    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3265" root="بلقع" body-key="b">
    
      Q. 3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِبْلَنْقَعَ</span></b>  <i>It</i> (sorrow, grief, or anxiety, such
as is termed <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَرْب</span>,) <i>became removed,</i> or <i>cleared
away.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>It</i> (the dawn) <i>shone,</i> or <i>shone
brightly.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>It</i> (a thing) <i>appeared, and
came forth.</i> (TA.)

